Notes for New Leaders
Leadership Responsibilities	Individual Responsibilities
	•	Lead Meetings
	•	Coach Others/Mentoring
	•	Conduct Performance Reviews
	•	Delegate Work
	•	Interview and hire staff	•	Setup Schedules
	•	Focus on Job
	•	Develop Yourself

Being a leader is a career change and involves:
	•	Getting work done through others instead of doing it oneself
	•	Facing more complex tasks and responsibilities, that one did as an individual contributor.
	•	Being comfortable with ambiguity.
	•	Letting go of direct control.
	•	Having successful interactions with others; requires redefining relationships with former peers.

Best Practices for Leading Former Peers:
	•	Acknowledge that your relationship with former peers has changed
	•	Address the change in position immediately and openly
	•	Be willing to listen to and value other’s opinions, observations and inputs
	•	Use what you know about your former peers to excite, motivate and inspire them.


